---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import profilePicture from "../assets/profile-picture.jpg";
const pageTitle = "Bio";

const tools = [
  {
    label: "Supabase",
    to: "https://supabase.com/",
    description: "Cloud based database hosting",
  },
  {
    label: "PostgreSQL",
    to: "https://www.postgresql.org/",
    description: "Open source object relational database system",
  },
  {
    label: "Python",
    to: "https://www.python.org/",
    description:
      "General purpose programming language with machine learning and AI capabilities",
  },
  {
    label: "Ray",
    to: "https://docs.ray.io/en/latest/index.html",
    description: "Python framework to scale AI in cloud based systems",
  },
  {
    label: "FastAPI",
    to: "https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/",
    description: "Web framework for building APIs in Python",
  },
  {
    label: "React",
    to: "https://react.dev/",
    description:
      "Frontend JavaScript library for building quick web applications",
  },
  {
    label: "Astro",
    to: "https://astro.build/",
    description: "JavaScript framework for building my personal blog",
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout pageTitle={pageTitle}>
  <section>
    <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row items-center gap-4">
      <div class="w-full md:w-1/3 shrink-0">
        <Image
          src={profilePicture}
          alt="A photo of Justin Groves overlooking a lake."
          class="w-full rounded-full"
        />
      </div>
      <div
        class="flex flex-col justify-center items-center text-center w-full md:w-2/3 gap-6"
      >
        <h2 class="font-logo text-4xl small-caps">Justin Groves, PhD</h2>
        <p class="tag-line">Sr. Data Scientist & Machine Learning Enthusiast</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="flex justify-center items-center pt-5">
      <p class="tag-line text-3xl">
        The Doctor is in.
        <sup id="ref-1">
          <a href="#fn-1" class="text-xs link">1</a>
        </sup>
      </p>
    </div>

    <p>
      Problem solving is a core part of my work, and currently that includes
      taking messy data and translating it into business solutions. I work
      across all facets of the data lifecycle including engineering, analytics,
      and modeling.
    </p>

    <h2>What I Do</h2>

    <p>
      Currently I'm a Sr. Data Scientist with <a
        href="https://reefpointgroup.com/"
        target="_blank"
        class="link">ReefPoint Group</a
      >, a D.C. based government consulting firm. In my time I've worked
      extensively with Palantir Foundry and Microsoft Power Platform
      understanding the business needs of non-technical stakeholders and turning
      them into data-driven solutions for the VA.
    </p>

    <p class="tag-line">
      Check out <a target="_blank" class="link" href="/resume.pdf">my resume</a> to
      see my full breadth of experience.
    </p>

    <p>
      Some of my notable projects include building a classification model for
      detecting demographic collection points in VA forms and building out a
      full database management system (DBMS) with Microsoft Power Platform for
      tracking and analyzing
      <a href="https://pra.digital.gov/" target="_blank" class="link"
        >Paperwork Reduction Act (PRA)</a
      > collections as they move through the approval lifecycle.
    </p>

    <p>
      My background includes a PhD in Mathematics with a minor in Data Science &
      Statistics from <a
        class="link"
        target="_blank"
        href="https://math.utk.edu/">The University of Tennessee - Knoxville</a
      > where I researched applications of <a
        class="link"
        target="_blank"
        href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elliptic_curve">elliptic curves</a
      > to <a
        class="link"
        target="_blank"
        href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Error_correction_code"
        >error-correcting codes (ECC)</a
      >. You can read all about it in <a
        class="link"
        target="_blank"
        href="https://trace.tennessee.edu/handle/20.500.14382/29893"
        >my dissertation</a
      >.
    </p>

    <h2>What I Explore</h2>
    <p>
      My recent interests have been building full-stack systems leveraging
      modern framework tools, like
      <ul>
        {
          tools.map((tool) => (
            <li>
              <a href={tool.to}>{tool.label}</a> - {tool.description}
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </p>
    <p>
      There's no shortage of tools in the AI landscape, and I look for those
      that help people cut through all the noise and bloat to get to the heart
      of their problems. I continue to research and explore Natural Language
      Processing (NLP) and speech-to-text models (like Open AI's <a
        href="https://openai.com/index/whisper/"
        target="_blank"
        class="link">Whisper</a
      >) to extract insight from spoken word.
    </p>

    <div class="flex justify-center items-center">
      <p class="tag-line">
        The future is now, and data is the key to the lock.
      </p>
    </div>

    <hr class="my-8" />

    <ol class="text-xs">
      <li id="fn-1">
        Non-statistically significant results may vary.
        <a href="#ref-1" class="ml-2 link">↩</a>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
